            // 438, 785), through its temperature profile: 70.43 K at the tropopause at
            // 44 km, 186 K at the stratopause at 250 km, ~170 K in the upper atmosphere
            // (from 500 km; the same paper), linear between; 95.1 % N2, 4.9 % CH4 (Niemann
            // et al. 2005; M = 27.43 g/mol throughout, methane's fall above the troposphere
            // left out). This gives ~7e-10 kg/m3 at 1,000 km, where Cassini flew through
            // a few 1e-10. The table runs up to where the density is negligible
            // (~1e-14 kg/m3); `top` (live flight, rails floor) where it falls to ~2e-9 kg/m3. N2:
            // gamma 1.4, VHS collision diameter 4.17e-10 m (Bird 1994); Sutton-Graves for
            // the stratosphere and above, where entry heating peaks: 98.5 % N2, 1.5 % CH4
            // (methane's 1.48 % there, Niemann et al. 2005), by their mixing rule (TR R-376
